<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Kolhapur State</h1><p class="st-meta">1710 CE – 1949 CE (approx.) · capital Kolhapur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The senior surviving Maratha state of Shivaji's line, founded by Queen Tarabai and made famous by the social reformer Shahu Maharaj.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> succession dispute that followed the release of Shahu in 1707, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarabai">Tarabai</a>, widow of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajaram-i">Rajaram</a>, set up a rival court for her son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji-ii">Shivaji II</a>, settling at Kolhapur by around 1710. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-warna">Treaty of Warna</a> in 1731 divided the Maratha kingdom between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satara">Satara</a> and Kolhapur.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhatrapati">Chhatrapatis</a> of Kolhapur ruled the fertile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panchganga-river">Panchganga</a> valley. Shahu, who reigned from 1894 to 1922, founded schools and hostels, reserved posts for non-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> and backward <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste">castes</a> in 1902, and supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satyashodhak-samaj">Satyashodhak</a> movement. It was a nineteen-gun salute state.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Kolhapur merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bombay-presidency">Bombay Province</a> in 1949 and became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a> in 1960. The royal family remains influential in the city.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kolhapur-state.jpg" alt="Kolhapur State" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Robert Alfers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kolhapur_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1710 CE – 1949 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kolhapur</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tarabai, Shahu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Marathi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kolhapur</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1830&amp;focus=kolhapur-state" aria-label="Kolhapur State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6700 1557 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kolhapur State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7020 1813L6991 1757M7020 1813L7364 1601M7020 1813L7364 1602M7020 1813L7018 1386M7020 1813L7027 1813M7020 1813L7050 1674M7020 1813L7010 1819M7020 1813L7023 1818"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6991 1757h0M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0M7027 1813h0M7050 1674h0M7010 1819h0M7023 1818h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7020 1813h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7020 1813h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kolhapur. <a href="/atlas?year=1830&amp;focus=kolhapur-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
